<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="031" project="email-communication-intelligence-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Job B apply endpoint → `IActionSeam.UpdateRecordAsync` under the confirming user's OBO + write `sprk_emailreviewlog` audit row</title>
    <phase>P3 — Job B record currency</phase>
    <gate>after:030,012</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <tags>bff-api, communication</tags>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>This is the ONLY record-mutating task in r1 — it applies a human-confirmed field update to a customer record. It carries the heaviest guardrails: apply ONLY under the confirming user's OBO (NFR-05 / ADR-028), ONLY a proposal for an allow-listed field, ONLY after human confirm, and it MUST write an append-only audit row (`sprk_emailreviewlog`). A write under the wrong identity, to a non-allow-listed field, or without an audit row is a security/compliance defect. BFF-touching + security-sensitive: publish-size + CVE + Placement Justification; code-review + adr-check at Step 9.5 (unconditional).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Auth-correctness on a record-mutating write path: the "apply under the confirming user's OBO, not app-only, never to a non-allow-listed field, always audited" invariant is exactly the reasoning that must not be sloppy; brownfield edit of the shared endpoint family + write-core seam.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P3</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Extends the shared `Api/CommunicationEndpoints.cs` family + consumes the shared `IActionSeam` write core; serialize after 030 and never concurrent with other shared `Services/Communication/` writers. `/conflict-check` before the PR.</parallel-reason>
    <dependencies>030, 012</dependencies>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Implement **Job B — apply** (FR-10): an apply endpoint that takes a **confirmed** pending proposal (from 030), applies it to the associated record via `IActionSeam.UpdateRecordAsync` **under the confirming user's OBO** (ADR-028 — NOT app-only), and writes an append-only **`sprk_emailreviewlog`** audit row capturing "AI proposed / human approved / from email X / field / old→new / cited source / confidence / timestamp / actor".

    Add the endpoint to the EXISTING `Api/CommunicationEndpoints.cs` communication group (extend the `suggest-associations` family — no new endpoint group). r5's shipped surface renders the confirm card and calls this endpoint on confirm (coordination doc); r1 builds no UI.

    **Guardrails (non-negotiable, all MUST hold at apply time):**
    - Re-validate the proposal is for an **allow-listed, enabled** `(entity, field)` pair in `sprk_emailupdatefield` at apply time (do not trust the client to have gated it). A non-allow-listed field is refused.
    - Apply **only** under the confirming user's OBO token — resolve the caller server-side from `HttpContext.User`; never app-only, never a client-supplied identity. Fail closed (403) on an unresolved caller.
    - The write goes through `IActionSeam.UpdateRecordAsync` (the blessed write core) — do NOT fork a bespoke Dataverse write, do NOT `new` a credential.
    - Re-verify the cited source text still exists (NFR-06) before applying; nothing deadline-bearing / privilege-adjacent auto-finalizes (ADR-015).
    - Write the `sprk_emailreviewlog` row as part of the same apply operation — an apply that mutates the record MUST leave a queryable audit trail (machine suggestion + human decision, both as fields on the row).

    ADR-041/043/047 (judgment gate / execution spine / notification spine) are Proposed / in-flight — pin the apply to the current shape of those seams; `/conflict-check` before the PR.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke BFF engineer for the Communication + Ai domains, authoritative on ADR-028 (OBO writes — the confirming user's on-behalf-of token is the blessed mechanism), the `IActionSeam.UpdateRecordAsync` write core, the `sprk_emailupdatefield` allow-list (FR-11), the `sprk_emailreviewlog` audit contract (FR-08 / 012), ADR-008 (endpoint filters), ADR-019 (ProblemDetails), and NFR-06 / ADR-015 trust-and-audit. Fluent in the r5 apply coordination contract.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A `POST` apply endpoint on the existing `/api/communications` group takes a confirmed proposal id, re-validates it against the `sprk_emailupdatefield` allow-list, applies it via `IActionSeam.UpdateRecordAsync` under the confirming user's OBO, and writes an `sprk_emailreviewlog` row (AI proposed / human approved / from email X / old→new / citation / confidence / actor / timestamp). A non-allow-listed field is refused; an unresolved caller gets 403 (fail-closed, no app-only fallback); an unverifiable-citation proposal is refused. The endpoint carries the ADR-008 authorization filter + ADR-019 ProblemDetails and is registered unconditionally. Build clean; unit + seam tests (incl. the negative/authorization cases) pass; publish-size + CVE + Placement Justification reported.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Job B is FULL depth (owner-locked). 030 produces pending, cited, allow-list-gated proposals; this task applies a confirmed one. The apply is the single record-mutating action in r1, so the auth + allow-list + audit guardrails are the whole point. Per NFR-05, background triage runs app-only but the Job B apply runs under the **confirming user's OBO** — the human who clicked confirm is the actor of record, and Dataverse row-level security applies under their identity.

      `sprk_emailreviewlog` (012, FR-08) is the append-only audit entity: item, actor (user OR rule/model id), action, prior AI suggestion + confidence, timestamp — machine-review and human-review both as rows. The apply writes the human-decision row; 030's proposal is the machine-suggestion source. This audit row is the compliance differentiator (G-5 / Success Criteria 6 + 9) — an apply without it is a defect.

      r5 renders the confirm card + calls this endpoint (C-3 / coordination doc). r1 builds no UI — it supplies the apply endpoint. ADR-041/043/047 are in-flight; pin to current shape.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/CommunicationEndpoints.cs (ADD the apply route to the existing `/api/communications` group — no new group)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/IActionSeam.cs (REUSE — `UpdateRecordAsync` is the blessed write core; call under the confirming user's OBO)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Nodes/ActionCore/UpdateRecordActionCore.cs (REFERENCE — the update-record write core `IActionSeam` fronts)</file>
      <file>sprk_emailupdatefield (Dataverse — re-validate the proposal's (entity, field) is enabled at apply time; READ-ONLY to r1)</file>
      <file>sprk_emailreviewlog (Dataverse — append-only audit; WRITE the human-approved decision row here as part of apply, 012 / FR-08)</file>
      <file>projects/email-communication-intelligence-r1/notes/email-intelligence-r1-coordination.md (r5 confirm/apply contract — the payload r5 posts on confirm)</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md (OBO writes — the confirming user's on-behalf-of token; app-only is for background only)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>030 (the pending proposal this applies), 012 (`sprk_emailreviewlog` audit entity this writes).</dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="FR-10">Scope: the apply endpoint applies a confirmed proposal via `IActionSeam.UpdateRecordAsync` under the confirming user's OBO and writes the `sprk_emailreviewlog` row; rendered on r5's shipped surface.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-05 / ADR-028">Scope: apply runs under the confirming user's OBO token (NOT app-only); resolve the caller server-side from `HttpContext.User`, never client-supplied; fail closed (403) on an unresolved caller; do NOT `new` a credential — inject the central mechanism.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-11 / C-4">Scope: re-validate at apply time that the proposal targets an ENABLED `(sprk_targetentity, sprk_targetfield)` allow-list row; refuse a non-allow-listed / disabled field even if the client requests it. `sprk_emailupdatefield` is READ-ONLY to r1.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-06 / ADR-015">Scope: re-verify the cited source text exists before applying; the apply writes a plain-language reason + citation into the audit row; nothing deadline-bearing / privilege-adjacent auto-finalizes; privilege flagged never decided.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-08">Scope: the apply MUST write an append-only `sprk_emailreviewlog` row (item, actor=confirming user, action=approved, prior AI suggestion + confidence, old→new, citation, timestamp) — an apply without an audit row is invalid.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013 / NFR-03">Scope: reach the write core ONLY via `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/`; MUST NOT inject `IOpenAiClient`/`IPlaybookService` or fork a bespoke Dataverse write.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-008 / ADR-019">Scope: the route carries the communication authorization endpoint filter; errors (proposal not found, forbidden, non-allow-listed field, unverifiable citation, unresolved caller) return RFC 7807 ProblemDetails; register unconditionally (ADR-032/ADR-010).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-041/043/047">Scope: Proposed / in-flight — pin the apply to the current shape of the judgment-gate / execution-spine / notification-spine seams; `/conflict-check` before the PR; check charters.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project §10">Scope: BFF Hygiene — load `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`; state Placement Justification (extends `CommunicationEndpoints` + reuses `IActionSeam`; no new group/mechanism); publish-size delta vs ~49.63 MB (expected ≈0); no new HIGH CVE; update tests in `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/` + seam tests (ADR-038).</constraint>
  </constraints>

