  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`, ADR-028 (OBO write path), ADR-015 (privilege flagged never decided), the coordination doc (r5 confirm payload), and `DATA-ACCESS-DECISION-CRITERIA.md` (confirms BFF write, not Xrm.WebApi).</step>
    <step order="2">Read `CommunicationEndpoints.cs` (the `suggest-associations` family + auth filter shape), `IActionSeam.cs` (`UpdateRecordAsync` signature + how OBO is threaded), and 030's stored-proposal shape. Grep to confirm no existing apply route.</step>
    <step order="3">Implement the apply handler: load the confirmed proposal (030) → re-validate `(entity, field)` is enabled in `sprk_emailupdatefield` → re-verify the cited text exists → resolve the confirming caller from `HttpContext.User` (fail-closed 403 if unresolved) → call `IActionSeam.UpdateRecordAsync` under that caller's OBO.</step>
    <step order="4">Write the `sprk_emailreviewlog` row (item, actor=confirming user, action=approved, prior AI suggestion + confidence, old→new, citation, timestamp) as part of the same operation; an apply that mutates the record but fails to audit is a failure (surface it, do not silently succeed).</step>
    <step order="5">Add `POST /api/communications/{...}/apply` (or the coordination-doc-agreed route) to the existing `/api/communications` group: bind the proposal id/confirm payload, apply the ADR-008 authorization filter + ADR-019 ProblemDetails (not-found / forbidden / non-allow-listed / unverifiable-citation / unresolved-caller); register unconditionally (ADR-032/ADR-010).</step>
    <step order="6">Write unit + seam tests: (a) a confirmed allow-listed proposal applies under OBO and writes an `sprk_emailreviewlog` row; (b) NEGATIVE — a non-allow-listed / disabled field is REFUSED even when the client requests it; (c) NEGATIVE — the apply runs ONLY under the confirming user's OBO (never app-only), and an unresolved caller gets 403; (d) NEGATIVE — a proposal whose cited text no longer exists is refused; (e) an audit row is written on every successful apply. Follow ADR-038 (boundary mocks only; no banned patterns).</step>
    <step order="7">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` + targeted `dotnet test`; run publish-size (report absolute + delta vs ~49.63 MB) + CVE scan.</step>
    <step order="9.5">FULL-rigor gates (security-sensitive, unconditional): `code-review` (focus OBO-not-app-only, apply-time allow-list re-validation, audit-on-apply, no bespoke write); `adr-check` against ADR-028 / ADR-013 / ADR-015 + spec FR-10 / FR-11 / NFR-05 / NFR-06. Address Critical findings; cite Placement Justification.</step>
    <step order="10">Run `/conflict-check` before the PR (shared `Services/Communication/` + endpoint family; ADR-041/043/047 in-flight — pin to current shape).</step>
    <step order="11">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (031 ✅) + `current-task.md`; record decisions (apply route, OBO threading point, allow-list re-validation, audit-row shape).</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If applying under the confirming user's OBO surfaces an auth or judgment-gate ambiguity — e.g. the current ADR-028 OBO threading cannot be applied to `IActionSeam.UpdateRecordAsync` without app-only fallback, or the in-flight ADR-041 judgment gate's current shape conflicts with the confirm→apply contract — STOP and escalate per root §6 / §6.5. Do NOT fall back to app-only for the apply, and do NOT fork a bespoke write to work around the gate.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>The `suggest-associations` endpoint family is read-only; there is no route that applies a confirmed proposal. `IActionSeam.UpdateRecordAsync` owns the write core; `sprk_emailreviewlog` owns the audit; `sprk_emailupdatefield` owns the allow-list.</existing>
    <extension>Yes for the write mechanism (reuse `IActionSeam` — do not fork a bespoke Dataverse write); the route is new only because REST needs a new path to apply a confirmed proposal. No new service, no new write mechanism, no new auth mechanism.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without the apply endpoint, r5 has no way to apply a confirmed proposal and no record ever becomes current from email — FR-10 fails and the record-currency pillar (Success Criterion 6) does not ship; without apply-time allow-list re-validation + OBO + audit, an apply could mutate an arbitrary column under the wrong identity with no trail (security/compliance failure).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="read">Inspect the endpoint family, write-core seam, allow-list + audit contracts, coordination doc, ADR-028</tool>
    <tool name="grep">Confirm no existing apply route (§11); confirm no bespoke Dataverse write / app-only apply path introduced</tool>
    <tool name="edit">Add the apply route + handler; wire OBO + allow-list re-validation + audit-row write</tool>
    <tool name="bash">Build, unit/seam tests, publish-size, CVE scan</tool>
    <tool name="code-review">FULL-rigor security-sensitive gate (Step 9.5)</tool>
    <tool name="adr-check">FULL-rigor gate (Step 9.5)</tool>
    <tool name="conflict-check">Pre-PR hot-path scan (Step 10)</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/CommunicationEndpoints.cs (UPDATED — apply route on the existing group; OBO + allow-list re-validation + audit; unconditional; ADR-008/019)</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/ (UPDATED — apply handler consuming `IActionSeam.UpdateRecordAsync` under OBO + writing `sprk_emailreviewlog`)</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ + tests/integration/seam/ — apply-under-OBO + non-allow-listed-refused + app-only-never + unresolved-caller-403 + unverifiable-citation-refused + audit-row-written</output>
    <output type="docs">PR description with §11 Component Justification + bff-extensions Placement Justification + publish-size delta + CVE result</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">On confirm, a confirmed allow-listed proposal is applied to the associated record via `IActionSeam.UpdateRecordAsync` under the confirming user's OBO, and an `sprk_emailreviewlog` row records "AI proposed / human approved / from email X / old→new / citation / confidence / actor / timestamp".</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE (allow-list): a proposal targeting a non-allow-listed or disabled `(entity, field)` is REFUSED at apply time even when the client requests it (apply-time re-validation, not client-trusted).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE (auth): the apply runs ONLY under the confirming user's OBO — never app-only; an unresolved caller returns 403 (fail-closed, no app-only fallback); the caller is resolved server-side, never client-supplied.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE (citation): a proposal whose cited source text no longer exists is refused (NFR-06); nothing deadline-bearing / privilege-adjacent auto-finalizes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Every successful apply writes exactly one append-only `sprk_emailreviewlog` audit row; a mutate-without-audit path does not exist.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The write reuses `IActionSeam.UpdateRecordAsync` (no bespoke Dataverse write, no `new` credential); AI/write core reached only via `Services/Ai/PublicContracts/`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The route carries the ADR-008 authorization filter + ADR-019 ProblemDetails and is registered unconditionally; `dotnet build` clean; tests pass; publish-size delta ≈0 vs ~49.63 MB; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    The single most important properties are: apply under the confirming user's OBO (never app-only), refuse any non-allow-listed field at apply time, and always write the audit row. These are security/compliance-sensitive and non-negotiable. r5 renders the confirm card + posts to this endpoint (coordination doc); r1 builds no UI. ADR-041/043/047 in-flight — pin to current shape; `/conflict-check` before the PR.
  </notes>

